I've traced it to com.bumptech.glide.util.LruCache. After putting something in the cache it calls trimToSize, which iterates to evict items:

```java
 protected synchronized void trimToSize(int size) {
    Map.Entry<T, Y> last;
    while (currentSize > size) {
      last = cache.entrySet().iterator().next();
      final Y toRemove = last.getValue();
      currentSize -= getSize(toRemove);
      final T key = last.getKey();
      cache.remove(key);
      onItemEvicted(key, toRemove);
    }
  }
```

It decides to remove a key, as seen in this screenshot of a breakpoint after calling getKey() above:
![screen shot 2017-10-30 at 14 52 22](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1876063/32174412-0f95fbae-bd82-11e7-8b1a-1e9673bd1c9c.png)

It wants to remove it from the cache, but cache.remove(key) returns NULL, saying that it did not remove the key (maybe because it wasn't found?):
![screen shot 2017-10-30 at 14 52 34](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1876063/32174442-282c0d48-bd82-11e7-962f-76aaf878aa11.png)

In onItemEvicted it calls into ResourceRecycler, where the Resource is recycled but still referenced because it still lives in the cache, and then on the next trimToSize it crashes.

I tried changing trimToSize to use one instance of Iterator to iterate over the cache and also to remove instances, avoiding the use of keys:
```java
  protected synchronized void trimToSize(int size) {
    Map.Entry<T, Y> last;
    final Iterator<Map.Entry<T, Y>> cacheIterator = cache.entrySet().iterator();
    while (currentSize > size) {
      last = cacheIterator.next();
      final Y toRemove = last.getValue();
      currentSize -= getSize(toRemove);
      final T key = last.getKey();
      cacheIterator.remove();
      onItemEvicted(key, toRemove);
    }
  }
```

I couldn't get it to use my snapshot build of Glide so I couldn't try it out. It should make sure that the current item gets removed I guess?

